# What `rget' does with a member name the server chose.  This collection
# is under the Go server's -escapeprefix, so every PROPFIND in it names
# two members that are not names at all: one that unescapes to a path
# leaving the collection, and one with a Windows separator in it.
#
# rget is the only command that writes a local file under a name the
# server picked rather than one the user typed.  Without a check on
# those names it wrote outside the directory it was given.
lcd @WORK@
put hello.txt
ls
rget . back
quit
